{
 "schema": "chutes.tdx-gate.strict-json-numbers.v1",
 "rule": "a number is refused when it is not RFC 8259's grammar, or when its exact magnitude is 2^1024 - 2^970 or more (an IEEE 754 binary64 reads it as infinity); one that reads as zero is accepted. The rule is the same with or without a fraction or an exponent, and at any depth.",
